; Generated by proto (go run -C proto . cube), do not edit
; The corners of the cube on the screen for the first half of the animation, states 0-55 (every
; second frame from ZX frame 2829): per state the 8 vertices as x, y in 1/8 pixel of the
; 24x24 tile, vertex number x + 2y + 4z for the body corner at -1 or +1 on each axis. Frames
; between states are the mean of the two states. The second half of the animation is the
; image of the first, turned by 180 degrees. A face is seen when its corners run
; counterclockwise on the screen (clockwise for the faces at -1)
;
; The states are stored as state 0, the difference to state 1, and then for every further state the
; change of the difference (always -2 to 2, stored plus 2) as one nibble per value, the first
; value of a pair in the low nibble

